l  call it is going to equal move up  otherwise PDM will equal zero  subsequently if moved down is greater  than 0 and greater they move up then the  negative direction move nd M equals move  down or nd M equals 0  finally again so that was plus DM or  plus like positive move right we still  haven't gotten to our plus di or minus  di so or rather the what we've got now  is plus DM or minus DM and we still need  to get to di so we're gonna assume a  window of 14 days you can obviously pick  whatever window you want but the plus di  or PDI is we're going to call it equals  100 times the 14 exponential moving  average of PDM divided by ATR and the  ATR is that average true range so what  we did in the last video series last  mini-series rather then we have the  negative Direction index n di or minus  di as you'll see it chart it often is  going to be very similar 100 times the  14 exponential moving average of the nd  M divided by the ATR so that's your plus  di + - di lines on the chart and in a  little bit I'll show you an example of a  couple examples of this stuff being  charted subsequently we actually  calculate the ATX finally the ADX is the  100 times the 14 exponential moving  average of the absolute value so we're  just looking for the difference here as  a positive number the absolute value of  the positive directional index - the  negative directional index divided by  the PDI plus the NDI and what that's  basically going to do is smooth it out  and normalize the data so it's all  normalized across no matter what the  price of that stock or what the Forex  ratio is all that next this is basically  how you would write it probe programming  Li  so if you're gonna follow us all the way  through the programming of this this is  more of what you're gonna see otherwise  if you just want to conceptualize it in  your head this is maybe an easier way to  conceptualize it so now let's go ahead  and look at some examples and kind of  discuss this so let me bring up the  chart that will be charting on here and  the first one let's see I think it's all  set up to be a 14 let me just check to  make sure yes this will plot a 14 ATX  across the board and the 14 positive  directional index of negative let's  start with Tesla will just peak at Tesla  see at Tesla's then since we looked at  that just not too long ago so this is  what we got here and so as you can see  I'm just going to fit this to your  screen a little bit here so as you can  see this centre line here the white line  is our ATX line the ATX signal lines is  the strength of a trend so as you can  see this trend this upward trend as it  continued going up and it kind of  slumped here the strength of the trend  did change and so again the ATX line is  just the strength of the trend so it  looks like it's following this line but  as this line continues to drop this  strength will actually probably start  going back up again if it does continue  to drop so keep that in mind that this  isn't it's just the strength of the  trend then you have the green line which  is our plus dir PDI and that is whether  or not that trend is a positive trend or  it's a negative trend so if we zoom in  to another spot like let's let's ignore  what's going on out here and look at  some of these trends in here and so as  you can see that as this was happening  here you could see that this the  negative was kind of going up and it did  cross over the green but then I started  going right back up again and then by  atomic meets the top here the green was  back and you know shown its face but  then it was already too late  it was going down so keep that in mind  obviously you're gonna see stuff like  that a lot of times the crossover that  marks a buy or a sell point  so maybe with Tesla with such volatility  with Tesla here you wouldn't want to use  a 14-day range alright so let's go ahead  and take a peek at another stock so  maybe let's look at eBay eBay is another  one that's been pretty volatile so be  interesting to see ok so here is our  eBay chart fit to screen  so here's eBay again and so here we can  see again here whether this is actually  a downtrend and as it continues dropping  the trend strength theoretically goes up  and then it kind of Wiggles around here  and kind of confuses us so the trend  strength starts to decrease because it's  like well this is no longer as strong as  it once was and sure enough as it goes  down far enough we can see the trend  does indeed change not only that but we  can see here where the negative  directional index is very strong it's  much stronger than our positive as it  hits this bottom as it starts playing  around here you can see this starts  actually losing strength same time the  trend starts losing strength so now  we're getting a signal that maybe the  trend is about to change  sure enough we get all three crossing  over right about here where positive  comes over negative goes down and this  comes down and starts changing its mind  about the direction it's going sure  enough we do get an upward trend so  that's the idea again we can see it  happening right over here so we'll zoom  in to this spot and then as you can see  as this continues going up we've got the  trend strength continuing and we've got  the positive directional index holding  you know positive then we've got a  crossover here sure enough we can see  that it's no longer as strong and the  trend strength continues going down so  actually overall pretty an interest  pretty interesting system say the least  so now what we're going to go ahead and  do is learn how to program this system  and then I'll show you how to go ahead  and plot it up on a chart just like this  one as always thanks for watching thanks  for the support the subscriptions and  until the next video

